liability and crew atmosphere, despite communication issues. However, difficulty communicating ideas could affect crew cooperation, but positive atmosphere suggests good crew interaction. Egocentric and not willing to further education may affect adaptability.\n\nWe need to decide recommendation. Perhaps we can argue that C now appears stronger than B because of 100% reliability and positive crew atmosphere, and technical competence is solid. The communication concerns are less severe than B's nasty remarks. So we might shift vote to C.\n\nWe need to reference evidence: C's 100% reliability, creates positive atmosphere, understands complicated technology, makes correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, but difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nWe should also maybe ask about Candidate D's crew cooperation, but we can keep focus on C vs B.\n\nThus we can state: Based on combined evidence, I now recommend Candidate C. Provide reasoning.\n\nLet's produce public message: mention that James's info confirms technical competence, combine with reliability and crew atmosphere, note concerns but weigh them.\n\nVote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
