ut we don't have direct info on D's crew cooperation. We could say we lack that info, and ask James. But James is being asked. We could also comment on Candidate C vs B again, reinforcing our vote for C, and note that D's moodiness and loner traits raise concerns for crew cooperation, making C still preferred. Provide reasoning.\n\nThus public message: I agree with Sarah's request, but I can add that D's moody and loner reputation suggests potential crew cooperation issues, which further supports C. I maintain vote for C.\n\nWe need to include metadata vote: Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
